<title>FRANCE: AGF wants to take control of Coface.</title>
<headline>AGF wants to take control of Coface.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>French insurance group AGF wants to take control of Coface, the country's biggest export credit insurer, by buying the holdings of BNP and Societe Generale, an AGF spokeswoman said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;AGF is considering a plan for the purchase of these stakes, Talks are underway,&quot; she said, adding that the idea should take more concrete form next year.</p>
<p>AGF currently has 31 percent of Coface directly and 49.9 percent indirectly, while BNP and Societe Generale each had 5.5 percent in Coface.</p>
</text>
